   "fix": null,
   "harm": "In-memory index state advances ahead of persisted data during batching; an interrupt causes Commit() to write advanced state with a stale locator, corrupting the index on restart",
   "hash": "e3c48e8aa5ed71e6",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:25:13+00:00",
     "blocking": true,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "r:3744459738",
     "status": "open"
    }
   ],
   "id": "r:3744459738",
   "kind": "correctness",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "The most serious issue seems to me that `Commit()` during interrupt writes advanced `m_muhash` alongside a stale locator, which causes `CoinStatsIndex::CustomInit` to reject the index as corrupted on restart.",
   "settled_by": null,
   "status": "open",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/34489#pullrequestreview-3744459738"
  },
  {
   "association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
   "at": "2026-03-09",
   "author": "l0rinc",
   "author_replies": [
    "rc:2936981455",
    "rc:2940770445"
   ],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": null,
   "harm": "Commit claims to be a refactor with no behavior change but reorders iterator assignment before block processing without documenting the change or safety",
   "hash": "e659e283a858b58f",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:25:13+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:2905123979",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:2905123979",
   "kind": "correctness",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "We're changing behavior in a commit that claims it's not a behavior change, without adding context for why this change was needed",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2026-03-16",
    "by": "sipa",
    "id": "rc:2940970303",
    "quote": "It seems obvious to me that 95fc91fc99a14c6635c13ba7b6a8e7c2a1efe7be cannot change behavior"
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/34489#discussion_r2905123979"
